  "measurement_note": "Teacher-forced: every branch receives the frozen twelve-line plan prompt and the reference's saved plan. Label decisions compare the two label first tokens at each label position. Not free-generation accuracy. The reference cache is never edited; edited target caches change only result-region values.",
  "mechanism_note": "Under replacement the target row's attention weights come entirely from the reference row; its own queries and keys are unused. The transferred cache therefore acts on the target row only through values, including values B computes for its own tokens.",
  "stats_note": "Bootstrap resamples the nine source cases (2000 draws). Deltas are right minus left; cases_increased / cases_decreased give direction only (for errors and KL an increase is worse).",
  "tolerance": {
    "max_mean_kl": 0.01,
    "min_argmax_agree": 0.98,
    "labels_equal": true
  },
  "interpretation_guide": "A large drop under zeroed or permuted result values supports the view that, under the oracle, B still depends on the transferred result values. Little change means the reference's attention pattern can drive much of the answer by itself, and claims about B 'reading A's results' need to be more cautious. Both edits are artificial (zero values are off-distribution; permutation keeps the value distribution but breaks token-to-value correspondence), so neither alone is a semantic explanation. Teacher-forced; not free-generation accuracy."
